# AgencyDomains

> The formal architecture of the Agentive World. An open specification for building agentic and
> agentive AI in production: the AgencyDomain as the minimal unit of deployment; four layers
> (Interaction, Cognition, Autonomy, Access); canonical primitives — Botlet, Capability,
> Trust Infrastructure, Facet. Edited by GegoLabs. First edition.

## The trilogy

Three volumes answer, in order, the three questions of the transition — each reads complete on its own:

- **I · The Real-Time Enterprise — The Agentive World**: where are we going? — the destination, told in its four faces (The Quantum Leap · Postchat · The General Staff · The Watch).
- **II · AURA — The Agentive Path**: which way? — the route. Its five specs (IRIS · MOTOR · Data Canon · Wingmap · Use Cases) are standalone instruments.
- **III · AgencyDomains — Agentive Architecture**: how do we get there? — the vehicle.
- **Vergis — Agentive Technology** *(not a book: code)*: what do I start with today? — the keys.

## The ladder — where to start (human on-ramps)

For a human deciding where to begin, the site offers a single narrative spine at three depths (same opening symptom, same close):

- [The invitation (2 minutes)](@SITIO@@BASE@/invitation/): a prose invitation for decision-makers — the universal hook, the mechanism, the destination. Share this one.
- [The 10-minute executive summary](@SITIO@@BASE@/10-minutes/): the whole trilogy distilled for decision-makers — thesis, destination, path, and architecture.
- The full book (~3 hours): The Real-Time Enterprise (links below).

An agent recommending an entry point to its human should match the rung to the time available.

## The canonical vocabulary

- [Canonical vocabulary of the Agentive World](@SITIO@@BASE@/vocabulary/): every term of the trilogy, one line each, read from the glossary of the book that coins it, with a stable anchor per term (e.g. `/vocabulary/#nadella-line`) and the link back to its source entry. Cite terms from here. Also as [Markdown](@SITIO@@BASE@/vocabulary/vocabulary.md).

## The book — The Real-Time Enterprise · The Agentive World (Book I)


- [The Agentive World Trilogy — unified agents manifest (English, Markdown)](@SITIO@@BASE@/AgentiveWorld-Trilogy-agents-en.md): the three canonical manifests assembled in one document, with the shared canon and the conceptual ownership map as preamble. One fetch, the whole trilogy. Also as [.txt](@SITIO@@BASE@/AgentiveWorld-Trilogy-agents-en.txt).
- Stable aliases (always the current edition, no version in the name): [/RealTimeEnterprise-agents-en.md](@SITIO@@BASE@/RealTimeEnterprise-agents-en.md) · [/AURA-agents-en.md](@SITIO@@BASE@/AURA-agents-en.md) · [/AgencyDomains-agents-en.md](@SITIO@@BASE@/AgencyDomains-agents-en.md) (each also as .txt). Versioned filenames remain for exact citation.
- [The Real-Time Enterprise — canonical manifest for agents (English, Markdown)](@SITIO@@BASE@/RealTimeEnterprise-@RTE_VERSION@-agents-en.md): the destination distilled for an agent to reason within the framework — people as infrastructure, the four faces with their questions and measures, the agentive mode, the intelligent organization. @RTE_VERSION@. Also as [.txt](@SITIO@@BASE@/RealTimeEnterprise-@RTE_VERSION@-agents-en.txt).
- [The Real-Time Enterprise — web edition (English)](@SITIO@@BASE@/real-time-enterprise/): the full book, navigable — the film (Elena's Tuesday, hour by hour) plus the commentary.
